WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:04.113
One call, ten agents, and the answer moves.

00:00:04.113 --> 00:00:05.504
The batch is real.

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:06.896
It is not answer-preserving.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.977
The README, from aeluyo8-blip/jev-swarm: The model answers ten judgments in roughly

00:00:12.977 --> 00:00:14.860
the time of one.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.802
It holds.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.787
Jev_choice, 30 tickets grouped against one shared state.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:25.273
269 of 270: answers that agree with the baseline.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.416
−0.29 rubric levels jev_score moved when grouped, on a 0–3 scale.

00:00:31.416 --> 00:00:34.672
Six tickets, all moving the same way.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.514
Argmax survives the batch.

00:00:37.514 --> 00:00:39.656
The probability-weighted mean does not.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.858
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
